{"title":"2023 IOQM/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For n ∈ N , let P(n) denote the product of the digits in n and S(n) denote the\nsum of the digits in n . Consider the set\nA = {n ∈ N&#160;: P(n) is non-zero, square free and S(n) is a proper divisor of P(n) } .\nFind the maximum possible number of digits of the numbers in A .\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As P(n) is square free, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> does not contain the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4142f19e4ce12b7573b360338918f158930044a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 8, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, leaving us to select the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fc80df065847b7756a7fe9fd57f9702dd6bd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />. Moreover, due to this condition, the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8effbba9c83e52fc90ea5a0c3269f872dbbbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cannot appear in the same number. \n</p><p>To maximise the number of digits, we must maximise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. Note that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975c9038b1e8c252ed974c782c4806fb73079621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7 = 6 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7 = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"14\" />. Using this, we find that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is simply the largest proper divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. This maximum value can be obtained in two ways <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />: \nCase I: using the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/19602d94d877474a0e26c929000de190d69046bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 5, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> (where each digit is used exactly once). \nCase II: using the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/8103f271902015a63f40eb8ccb0ff9d504f5f56b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 5, 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> (where each digit is used exactly once). \n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32f1f94c3879095b39d33e8a3356accf93bdd7e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 &gt; 2+3+5+7, 6 + 5 + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"17\" />, meaning these digits alone do not reach the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. In order to reach this value, however, we can simply add a certain number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s to the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, ensuring the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, is unchanged. In Case I, number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75930f98808f5189854039f65fd75df09f70086e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 - (2 + 3 + 5 + 7) = 88$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />; in Case II, number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5214430bc8fada5118b096e39242ea4293f747f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 - (6 + 5 + 7) = 87$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />. Observe that Case I leads to the maximum number of overall digits, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab927757095dcc7b3b4051e507174aa7d42ca47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 88 = \\boxed{92}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~biggest_glitter_hater\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017091405\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 89/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4999/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25555:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017091405 and revision id 290687. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}